#
# models.manifest — the models ZXV.app may fetch on first run, read by
# zxv-model-fetch.sh. Copied into ZXV.app/Contents/Resources, so it is
# covered by the app's code signature: the sha256 pinned here is what makes
# a download from any IPFS gateway trustworthy.
#
# One model per line, fields separated by spaces or tabs:
#
#   NAME.gguf  SHA256(64 hex)  BYTES  CID  LICENCE
#
#   NAME     file name to install as (letters, digits, . _ -; ends .gguf)
#   SHA256   sha256 of the whole file, checked before it is installed
#   BYTES    exact size, checked too
#   CID      the file's IPFS CID (from the release's boot manifest)
#   LICENCE  SPDX id of the weights' licence, shown to the user; only
#            weights licensed for redistribution and commercial use belong
#            here (see docs/ARCHITECTURE_OVERVIEW.md gap 17)
#
# The first line that downloads and verifies is installed; the rest are
# fallbacks. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# This file is intentionally empty of entries: no model has been pinned
# for release yet, and an unpinned or invented CID must never ship. Until
# then the app offers "Choose GGUF File" instead, or a model bundled at
# build time with ZXV_BUNDLE_MODEL (see docs/MAC_APP.md).
